{"name":"China Pattern","hex":"#3d5c77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"china","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of porcelain, a hard white translucent ceramic made from kaolin, now  sometimes distinguished in reference to tableware as fine or good china.","Chinaware: porcelain tableware."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/china"},{"term":"pattern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Model, example.\nSomething from which a copy is made; a model or outline. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Something from which a copy is made; a model or outline. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply a pattern.","To make or design (anything) by, from, or after, something that serves as a pattern; to copy; to model; to imitate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pattern"}],"entries":[{"title":"China","blocks":[{"text":"China, officially the People's Republic of China (PRC), is a country in East Asia. It is divided into 33 province-level divisions, including two special administrative regions. Beijing is the capital, while Shanghai is the most populous city by urban area. Its geography features the Central Plain, major rivers such as the Yangtze and Yellow River, deserts, subtropical and temperate forests, plateaus, and mountain ranges such as the Himalayas. It is the world's second-most populous country after India, with a population exceeding 1.4 billion. Covering 9.6 million square kilometers (3,700,000 sq mi), it is the third largest country by area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China"},{"title":"Pattern","blocks":[{"text":"A pattern is a regularity in the world, in human-made design, or in abstract ideas. As such, the elements of a pattern repeat in a predictable and logical manner. There exists countless kinds of unclassified patterns, present in everyday nature, fashion, many artistic areas, as well as a connection with mathematics. A geometric pattern is a type of pattern formed of repeating geometric shapes and typically repeated like a wallpaper design."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Ionic_frieze_from_the_Erechtheum%2C_dimensions_130_x_50_cm%2C_in_the_Glyptothek.jpg/330px-Ionic_frieze_from_the_Erechtheum%2C_dimensions_130_x_50_cm%2C_in_the_Glyptothek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pattern"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219959.jpg/500px-MET_DP219959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219959.jpg/1280px-MET_DP219959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219959.jpg/500px-MET_DP219959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A set of Western Zhou-era ritual bronzes, c. 1000 BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMET_DP219959.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Terracotta_Army_%286143564816%29.jpg/500px-Terracotta_Army_%286143564816%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Terracotta_Army_%286143564816%29.jpg/1280px-Terracotta_Army_%286143564816%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Terracotta_Army_%286143564816%29.jpg/500px-Terracotta_Army_%286143564816%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped